  "status": "implemented and294distinct component cases pass; normal-feature runtime rebuild and regression recovery pending",
  "recorded_at": "2026-10-28T01:39:51.403420+00:00",
  "motivation": {
    "current_runtime": "docs/evidence/gate-6/canonical-ingress-policy-snapshot.json",
    "observed": "Snapshot build97 passes33native cases and3/4normal browser profiles(all8tone checks pass), but WT has4/15passes: all media journeys fail, mostly VP8 fragment loss. ChromeES256 cadence remains failed.",
    "mechanism": "NativePeerMedia intentionally drops capacity refusals. Newly nonblocking fresh model admission returns Backpressure on transient model mutex contention. Controlled cases reproduce initial and post-policy model collisions on real ports; prior implementation fails all7new recovery/expiry/authorization regressions.",
    "limitation": "The controlled defect is established; only a new actual runtime cohort can determine restoration of the observed WT/media scope or resolution of cadence failures."
  },
  "implementation": [
    "Fresh non-data ingress without borrowed packet context recovers model metadata for at most one20ms mix quantum. The original frame and frozen stream/credential/consumer/scene snapshots remain unchanged; no added packet queue or wire retry exists.",
    "If metadata collides after external policy admission, destroy that policy lease before waiting. Reacquire metadata, verify original model/credential, release metadata, then read current policy again; never cache a positive grant through the wait.",
    "Keep the earliest policy/credential IO deadline across all attempts. An expired original is never renewed by a later grant. Already expired task/principal remains Authority; a valid original whose IO lease expires remains Deadline.",
    "Retained/context-bearing/data/held paths retain existing behavior. The original global packet age and all current authorization, audience and IO fences remain; native capacity drop remains explicit when bounded recovery cannot finish."
  ],
